Based on the image you provided, your project structure still uses the old MOCService package names, but the code I gave you uses the new JournalService package names.
To fix this without errors, you need to rename each package in Eclipse.
Step-by-Step Renaming Instructions
In your Project Explorer (the left side of your screen shown in the image), right-click on each package listed below, select Refactor > Rename (or press Alt + Shift + R), and change the name as follows:
 * Config Package:
   * Old Name: com.tcs.fincore.MOCService.config
   * New Name: com.tcs.fincore.JournalService.config
 * Controllers Package:
   * Old Name: com.tcs.fincore.MOCService.Controllers
   * New Name: com.tcs.fincore.JournalService.Controllers
 * Dto Package:
   * Old Name: com.tcs.fincore.MOCService.Dto
   * New Name: com.tcs.fincore.JournalService.Dto
 * Exception Package:
   * Old Name: com.tcs.fincore.MOCService.Exception
   * New Name: com.tcs.fincore.JournalService.Exception
 * Models Package:
   * Old Name: com.tcs.fincore.MOCService.Models
   * New Name: com.tcs.fincore.JournalService.Models
 * Enums Package: (This might move automatically when you rename Models, but check it)
   * Old Name: com.tcs.fincore.MOCService.Models.enums
   * New Name: com.tcs.fincore.JournalService.Models.enums
 * Repository Package:
   * Old Name: com.tcs.fincore.MOCService.Repository
   * New Name: com.tcs.fincore.JournalService.Repository
 * Service Package:
   * Old Name: com.tcs.fincore.MOCService.Service
   * New Name: com.tcs.fincore.JournalService.Service
Important Checks
 * The Top Package: I see you already have a package named com.tcs.fincore.JournalService. Ensure your main application file (JournalServiceApplication.java) is inside this package.
 * Test Folder: At the bottom of your image, under src/test/java, you also have com.tcs.fincore.MOCService. Rename that to com.tcs.fincore.JournalService as well.
Why do this via Refactor?
When you use Refactor > Rename in Eclipse, it automatically updates the package line at the top of every Java file inside those folders, saving you from manually editing hundreds of lines of code. Once you do this, the code I provided earlier will fit perfectly.
